{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>For, and a mouth of deceit</b> — <b>and a mouth of a man of deceit</b>, like <b>do not be rebellious</b> (Proverbs 19:3); and 'mouth' is active for the word <b>they have opened</b>, as if it were written: For the wicked and a man of deceit have opened their mouth against me."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 109, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:08.817563867Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}